WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.225 --> 00:00:04.975
At the wholesale desk, the next supplier quote needs a comparable market reference.

2
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:13.413
With ProduceWatch, start with your team's watchlist: the exact pack, origin and market basis you use.

3
00:00:16.237 --> 00:00:22.400
Review comparable ranges and the week to date view. Keep source dates and missing observations visible.

4
00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:33.750
Read shipment context alongside prices, with source corrections clearly separated from market changes.

5
00:00:36.238 --> 00:00:42.125
Review your quote. A shipping point reference is not a delivered offer. Freight and terms still matter.

6
00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:52.575
Carry the same reference into one report, with source notes intact and private quotes kept separate.

7
00:00:55.225 --> 00:01:02.900
Use team email, PDF or spreadsheets. Or agree a JSON, XML or webhook route for your system.

8
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:08.712
Start with one buying desk and supported sources. Ask about a scoped ProduceWatch pilot.
